{"id":"s1","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":1,"of":10,"title":"Joining clauses","titleHe":"מִשְׁפָּט מְחֻבָּר","goal":"Use שֶׁ, כִּי and כְּדֵי to build sentences longer than one clause.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"שֶׁ is the workhorse. Glued to the front of a clause it does the job of English that, which and who all at once — and unlike English, it is never optional."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי חוֹשֵׁב שֶׁהוּא צוֹדֵק.","en":"I think (that) he's right."},{"he":"הָאִישׁ שֶׁבָּא אֶתְמוֹל","en":"the man who came yesterday"},{"he":"הַסֵּפֶר שֶׁקָּרָאתִי","en":"the book (that) I read"},{"he":"כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי, הוּא כְּבָר הָלַךְ.","en":"When I arrived, he'd already left."}]},{"type":"table","caption":"Connectors","head":["Hebrew","English"],"rows":[["שֶׁ","that, which, who"],["כִּי","because"],["כְּדֵי","in order to"],["אֲבָל","but"],["לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","before"],["אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","after"],["בִּגְלַל שֶׁ","because of the fact that"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"אֲשֶׁר is שֶׁ in literary dress — same meaning, separate word, and everywhere in older prose. When you meet it, read it as שֶׁ."}],"vocab":[{"he":"שֶׁ","en":"that, which, who","translit":"she-"},{"he":"כִּי","en":"because","translit":"ki"},{"he":"אֲשֶׁר","en":"that, which (literary)","translit":"asher"},{"he":"כְּדֵי","en":"in order to","translit":"kdei"},{"he":"אֲבָל","en":"but","translit":"aval"},{"he":"לָכֵן","en":"therefore","translit":"lachen"},{"he":"לְמָשָׁל","en":"for example","translit":"lemashal"},{"he":"בְּעֶצֶם","en":"actually","translit":"be'etsem"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["belief, faith","secret","that, which, who","wait! (m.)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שֶׁ","translit":"she-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["because","fails","train","dirty"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כִּי","translit":"ki"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["children","that, which (literary)","(marks a definite object)","requests"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֲשֶׁר","translit":"asher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["ceiling","in order to","meaning","rejoicing"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כְּדֵי","translit":"kdei"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["promises","was born","firmament, sky","but"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֲבָל","translit":"aval"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["therefore","aunt","hope","forest"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לָכֵן","translit":"lachen"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["for example","books","twelve (f.)","lest"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לְמָשָׁל","translit":"lemashal"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “because”?","options":["שְׁאֵלָה","מַדָּע","שָׁכֵן","כִּי"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אֲשֶׁר","translit":"asher","en":"that, which (literary)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “for example”?","options":["לְמָשָׁל","בֵּיתוֹ","נֶכְדָּה","בִּכְלָל"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["שֶׁ","that, which, who"],["כִּי","because"],["אֲשֶׁר","that, which (literary)"],["כְּדֵי","in order to"],["אֲבָל","but"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “in order to”?","options":["מוּזָר","קָשֶׁה","כְּדֵי","דַּוְקָא"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אֲנִי ___ שֶׁהוּא צוֹדֵק.","en":"I think (that) he's right.","options":["כִּי","חוֹשֵׁב","שֶׁ","אֲשֶׁר"],"correct":1,"full":"אֲנִי חוֹשֵׁב שֶׁהוּא צוֹדֵק."},{"type":"build","tokens":["הוּא","הָלַךְ","כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי,","כְּבָר"],"answer":["כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי,","הוּא","כְּבָר","הָלַךְ"],"en":"When I arrived, he'd already left."},{"type":"build","tokens":["הָאִישׁ","אֶתְמוֹל","שֶׁבָּא"],"answer":["הָאִישׁ","שֶׁבָּא","אֶתְמוֹל"],"en":"the man who came yesterday"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “but” in Hebrew","answer":"אֲבָל","hint":"aval"}]}